!id: tfFUmGwnVe
!front: Euler's Formula
!back:
\[
\begin{align*}
  e^{ix}  &= \cos x + i \sin x \\
  e^{-ix} &= \cos x - i \sin x
\end{align*}
\]
~~~

!tags: Definition

!id: 8x5YMmQyYQ
!front: Mean Value Theorem
!back:
The **Mean Value Theorem** states that if a function \( f \) is:

- continuous on \( [a,b] \)
- differentiable on \( (a,b) \)

then there exists at least one \( c \in (a,b) \) such that the instantaneous rate of change at \( c \) equals the average rate of change over \( [a,b] \):
\[ f'(c) = \frac{f(b) - f(a)}{b - a}. \]
!extra:
Geometrically: there is at least one point on the curve where the tangent line is parallel to the secant line connecting the endpoints of the curve.

![Mean Value Theorem](mean_value_theorem.svg)
~~~

!type: Cloze Math
!tags: Algebra Identity

!id: QLE5oiqwbb
!text: \[ {{c2::(a + b)^2::\ldots}} = {{c1::a^2 + 2ab + b^2::\ldots}} \]
!related:
\[
\begin{align*}
  (a + b)^2 &= a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\
  (a - b)^2 &= a^2 - 2ab + b^2
\end{align*}
\]
~~~

!id: uB9DCIo1rD
!text: \[ {{c2::(a - b)^2::\ldots}} = {{c1::a^2 - 2ab + b^2::\ldots}} \]
!related:
\[
\begin{align*}
  (a + b)^2 &= a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\
  (a - b)^2 &= a^2 - 2ab + b^2
\end{align*}
\]
~~~
